MIB (MEN IN BLACK)
Creating Health Monitoring Software for Space Missions
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CORE CONCEPT:
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
To create an intelligent health assessment and monitoring system for space missions.
In other words, the goal is to design and develop a practical, applicable solution to the issue that astronauts sometimes overlook their own health.
This encompasses factors
such as radiation exposure, blood oxygen concentration, heart rate, VO2 max, bone health (gravity affects bone strength), hydration, and sleep quality.


NASA Open Data
NASA Open Data Portal (Thousands of datasets)
NASA Worldview (Daily, real-time satellite imagery)
Earthdata Search (Climate, atmospheric, and oceanic telemetry)
Partner Agencies (Data from ESA, JAXA, CSA, and others)
